  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:sefgphqp2xqwh2hawaixykwz/app.bsky.feed.post/3myphka2iyk2o",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Someone reverse engineered their Samsung TV using codex. They found that Samsung TVs were using always on mics, network mapping, and all kinds of Spyware that would collect data and sell it to data brokers.\n\nA day later, their openai account was banned and frontier labs cracked down on doing this.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myphka2iyk2o",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T14:53:29.594Z",
      "likes": 4441,
      "replies": 113,
      "reposts": 1818,
      "score": 10.3,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 3.8,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 16.9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myqfelxuxs2q",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "My general advice for using AI for any purpose is to ask yourself: \"how do I make what I am doing even more ambitious?\"\n\nYou do this over and over until you either hit a wall and thus learn the shape of the jagged frontier (useful!) or you find out that the AI can do more than you think (common!)",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myqfelxuxs2q",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T23:47:13.028Z",
      "likes": 160,
      "replies": 6,
      "reposts": 13,
      "score": 7.4,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mynwzdkgwc2m",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "An OpenAI researcher (Noam Brown) was generally mocked last month for suggesting that even air-gapped AI models on separate computers would find a way to communicate with each other, perhaps through CPU temperature changes. Given this latest report from OpenAI, it doesn’t seem so implausible.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mynwzdkgwc2m",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-25T00:25:03.233Z",
      "likes": 153,
      "replies": 20,
      "reposts": 16,
      "score": 7.1,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.3,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 31.4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3myjcs6g7zc2q",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "By every measure, Opus 4.8 beats human experts as peer reviewers in a study of 124 Harvard social science papers covering a range from statistical analyses to formal models to qualitative work.\n\nAs academics, we need to figure out how to adapt the practice of science to AI, and we need to do it fast",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3myjcs6g7zc2q",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-23T04:12:29.185Z",
      "likes": 193,
      "replies": 13,
      "reposts": 43,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.4,
        "recency": 0.6,
        "age_hours": 75.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3mylmyrsus226",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "There is a lot of interest from all the big AI labs on character steering, personas, etc. including Anthropic. I think it is poorly understood. @natolambert.bsky.social could probably say more. I’m not sure the Claude persona was intentional, but it is sort of a brand at this point, Ala Claudisms.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3mylmyrsus226",
